.TH CODEX-LB-STATUS 1 "September 2026" "codex-lb-status 0.1.36" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex-lb-status \- monitor Codex LB quota and account status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codex-lb-status
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codex-lb-status
is a read-only Ubuntu tray companion for Codex LB. It displays pooled quota,
account health, reset credits, and update state without keeping the dashboard
open.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session. Starting the command again presents
the requested window in the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start with only the tray indicator visible.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Start the indicator and present the Settings dialog.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/codex-lb-status/config.json
User preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/codex-lb-status/sessions/
Per-origin dashboard session cookies.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.victorstatko.codex_lb_status.desktop
User-created launch-at-login entry.
.SH SECURITY
Remote servers require HTTPS. Plain HTTP is accepted only for loopback
addresses. The application does not implement account, routing, quota, or
server-administration operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation is installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/codex-lb-status/README.md.gz .
.SH BUGS
Report non-security issues at
https://github.com/VictorStatko/codex-lb-status/issues.
